  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 10,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.438,
            0.069,
            0.817,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Orienting Yourself: The Use of Coordinates"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.855,
            0.069,
            0.883,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.886,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It makes no difference whether "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( X _ { _ 2 } - X _ { _ 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( y _ { _ 2 } - y _ { _ 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are positive or negative, as we are simply measuring the shifts along the two axes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.146,
            0.887,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What if, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X_{1}, X_{2}, Y_{3}, Y_{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " take negative values? In Fig. 1.9, triangle AMD is reflected in the y-axis. What are the coordinates of the images of points A, M, and D?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.209,
            0.883,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.114,
                0.209,
                0.883,
                0.506
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.543,
            0.815,
            0.562
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{CD}^{\\prime}=\\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{coordinate}-\\mathrm{of} \\mathrm{A}^{\\prime}-\\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{coordiintate},\\mathrm{of} \\mathrm{D}^{\\prime}=-3-(-7)=4."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.567,
            0.796,
            0.588
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{AC}^{\\prime}=\\mathrm{y-coordinate of A}^{\\prime}-\\mathrm{y-coordinate of D}^{\\prime}=4-1=3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.592,
            0.883,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the Baudhāyana–Pythagoras Theorem, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AD} = \\sqrt{4^{2} + 3^{2}} = 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.631,
            0.661,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can similarly calculate both D'M' and M'A':"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.337,
            0.659,
            0.661,
            0.685
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{D}^{\\prime} \\mathrm{M}^{\\prime}=\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+5^{2}}=\\sqrt{29} \\text { units }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.336,
            0.699,
            0.662,
            0.723
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{M^{\\prime}A^{\\prime}} = \\sqrt{(-6)^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{40}   units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.731,
            0.886,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that reflection has preserved the lengths of the sides of the triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.789,
            0.401,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.827,
            0.857,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. What has remained the same and what has changed with this reflection?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.869,
            0.857,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Would these observations be the same if ΔADM is reflected in the x-axis (instead of the y-axis)?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
